  "answer": "This has been requested before, and PowerToys doesn't show a CPU temperature in the bar next to the CPU and Memory icons. The closest match is #46434. It asks for temperature readings in the Command Palette Dock, which is where the CPU and Memory stats appear. A contributor said Windows has no native way to read per-component CPU temperature, because that needs vendor-specific drivers or WMI. They planned a pull request that adds one thermal-zone heat metric from PDH to the dock. It isn't confirmed as released, so check your PowerToys version and its release notes, and follow #46434 for updates. Until it ships, use a separate hardware-monitor tool to read CPU temperature. Issue #8433 says the same: the feature is still missing, and you'd need Dev Home or another tool. A taskbar version of this request (#35623) was closed as a duplicate of the general taskbar-integration issues."
 },
